# The Fedora family's package names for spark-shell (dnf). Fedora, and
# what says ID_LIKE=fedora (RHEL, Rocky, AlmaLinux: by family, not
# proven). A name counts as installed when any installed package provides
# it (rpm -q --whatprovides). No starship package here: the rc files draw
# the shell's own prompt. Every name was looked up in Fedora 44's package
# listing, and CI looks them up again on Fedora itself.
PM=dnf
PKG_SHELL=bash tmux ncurses diffutils
PKG_CLI=bat eza fzf zoxide fd-find jq btop
# curl and ssh-keygen: the dialog, fetched for a release tag whose signature is checked
# swayidle and swaylock: the display off and the lock when idle; grim, slurp and
# wl-clipboard: screen capture, to a file and the clipboard
# brightnessctl and ddcutil: the brightness, a laptop's backlight or a screen's DDC/CI
# librsvg2-tools is rsvg-convert: a drawing drawn again in another palette, a picture's colors read
# (gdk-pixbuf's thumbnailer is gone from Fedora's gdk-pixbuf2)
# mesa-dri-drivers: the GPU's own driver for sway, which a minimal install may lack
# no package of Monaspace Neon, the terminal's font, here: spark-shell on fetches the release's zip, its sha256 pinned
# mako: the notifications, and libnotify is notify-send; udisks2: a drive
# plugged in, mounted when asked
# poppler-utils is pdftoppm, pdfinfo and pdftotext: a PDF's page in a preview (#120)
# Xwayland: X11 apps, Steam and its games among them (#170); xrandr names the main screen
# X11's primary output, the first screen a Wine game takes (#173)
# the moving wallpaper (#180, #187, #188): mpv makes the loops, mpv-libs is the library the wallpaper
# player plays them through, numpy draws the scenes. Fedora's mesa-dri-drivers carries the VA-API
# driver but leaves H.264 out, so the loops decode on the CPU there unless RPM Fusion's driver is added
PKG_DESKTOP=sway swaybg foot foot-terminfo dejavu-sans-mono-fonts mesa-dri-drivers curl openssh-clients swayidle swaylock grim slurp wl-clipboard brightnessctl ddcutil librsvg2-tools poppler-utils mako libnotify udisks2 xdg-desktop-portal xdg-desktop-portal-wlr xdg-desktop-portal-gtk gsettings-desktop-schemas bluez python3-dbus python3-gobject xorg-x11-server-Xwayland xrandr mpv mpv-libs python3-numpy wtype
# the sound with the desktop: PipeWire, WirePlumber, its PulseAudio server
# and ALSA programs through it (Bluetooth sound is in pipewire-libs, which pipewire pulls)
PKG_SOUND=pipewire wireplumber pipewire-pulseaudio pipewire-alsa
# kbd is setvtrgb and setfont, the console palette and font
PKG_CONSOLE=kbd
# the login screen (spark-shell on login): greetd, swayidle to turn the display
# off when idle, and the account greetd's package makes for it. Where SELinux
# is on, dnf brings greetd-selinux with greetd (the package asks for it)
PKG_LOGIN=greetd swayidle
LOGIN_ACCOUNT=greetd
